   <title>Africa&#039;s first Youth Olympics open in Senegal amid hope and scrutiny</title>
   <link>https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss</link>
   <description>Senegal is hosting Africa&#039;s first Youth Olympics, with 2,700 young athletes competing in Dakar, Diamniadio and Saly. The Games bring pride and hope, but also questions over cost, rights and legacy.</description>
